Add No Courier/Collection couriers, a Couriers settings section, and
APC Overnight integration (v0.126)

Dan asked for three things together: a "No Courier" option that hides
the service box entirely, an admin-extensible "Collection" courier
category (Customer/UKI/InXpress/Seabridge to start) for external
couriers BNS neither books nor labels, and full APC Overnight
integration via the Hypaship Booking Platform API v3 (docs attached),
with its settings living alongside DPD's in a new Couriers section.

The underlying gap this closes: courier was never actually a
persisted field on Order - "DPD" was hardcoded as the only option in
the frontend dropdown, and which courier had shipped was only ever
inferred from whether a DPD shipment existed. That worked while DPD
was the only integration, but couldn't hold a second one. Order now
has a real `courierType` (NONE/DPD/APC/COLLECTION), backfilled on
existing orders from their DPD data.

Implemented:

- `CourierType` enum + `Order.courierType`/`collectionCourierName`,
  mirrored onto `Shipment` so archived shipments (Reverse to Despatch,
  additional part-shipments) keep their courier data too.
- `collection_courier_options` table + admin CRUD (Settings >
  Couriers > Collection Services, saves immediately per change) and a
  public active-only endpoint for the order screen's dropdown.
- New "Couriers" Settings section: the Collection Services list, then
  DPD's existing settings moved in unchanged, then a new APC block
  (email/password login - APC's auth is a simple Basic-style header,
  not DPD's OAuth token exchange - environment, account number,
  optional override collection address, default product code/goods
  description).
- `ApcAuthService`/`ApcShippingService`, structured like
  `DpdAuthService`/`DpdShippingService`: book an order (`Orders.json`)
  and fetch its label live on demand (ZPL, so it goes through the same
  print-agent flow as DPD labels), both best-effort and deliberately
  not `@Transactional` so a courier-side failure never blocks the
  despatch it's attached to.
- `DespatchService` books an APC shipment automatically at despatch
  time under the same conditions DPD already does (courier selected +
  credentials configured), and the despatch-confirmation status/colour
  coding now reflects whichever courier actually applies.
- OrderEdit's Despatch panel is now a real 4-way branch on
  `courierType`: nothing for No Courier, DPD unchanged, a plain
  dropdown with no booking/label UI for Collection, and an APC block
  mirroring DPD's (service picker with free-text fallback, book
  button, then waybill + print label).
- Delivery History's Courier column now reads the explicit
  `courierType` instead of guessing "DPD or nothing" from a
  consignment number - the same implicit-inference bug the rest of
  this change was fixing, so worth closing here too.

Deliberately out of scope for this first APC pass: tracking, amending
and cancelling a booked order, and a live product-code lookup
(APC's optional Service Availability call) - booking + label is what
despatch actually needs, matching what DPD parity requires. A short
static list of common product codes (ND10/ND12/ND16/NDSAT/ECO48) with
a free-text override covers the rest for now.

